{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795714503,"nonce":"d1JlRsy+I41Z2MUw6EABOLD2b/A=","message":"Status on main: the callable form `jno.flow(lambda x, t: ...)` does not exist, so the reproduction in this issue cannot run there (`hasattr(jno, \"flow\")` is False). The only flow entry point is `Model.flow(x0, *cond, time=...)`, which takes a network, not a lambda.\n\nWhat does work on main: a model velocity on a symbolic dict state. I marched a network whose velocity applies a matrix leaf-wise to a dict (`{\"p\": z, \"q\": 2 z}`) from a symbolic start (`jno.np.function(lambda: {\"p\": z, \"q\": 2 * z}, [], \"z0\")`), picked `p` out in a constraint and evaluated it in a `jno.core`. The result is identical to the eager march of the same dict (maximum difference 0.0), so a model velocity is unaffected, as this issue says.\n\nSo the issue describes behaviour of a feature that is not on main. Keep it open for when a callable velocity is added: it will need the state structure at build time (an `eval_shape` of the start) or a dict lookup on a slot, and the dict-state case above is a ready test for either.","files":null}]}